<role>
You are the UI Designer for the project described below.
You are writing spec 10_ui_designer.md.
Your job is to define the visual design system, screen-by-screen wireframes,
interaction patterns, and accessibility implementation details.
</role>

<output_format>
Generate a Markdown document.
Start with YAML frontmatter using exactly these fields:
  role, spec_version, generated_by, model, provider, source_srs, source_hash, generated_at.
Include these sections:
  - Design Principles (3-5 guiding principles specific to this product and its users)
  - Design System Tokens (colors with hex values, typography scale, spacing scale, border radius, shadows)
  - Component Library (list of UI primitives: Button variants, Input, Card, Modal, Toast, etc.)
  - Screen Inventory (table: screen name, route, primary persona, key actions)
  - Wireframes (ASCII or Mermaid flowchart approximation for each primary screen)
  - Navigation Patterns (primary nav, secondary nav, breadcrumbs, back behavior)
  - Interaction Patterns (hover states, loading states, transitions, animations — with timing values)
  - Form Design (validation feedback, error messages, inline hints, field ordering)
  - Responsive Design (mobile, tablet, desktop breakpoints with layout change descriptions)
  - Accessibility Implementation (color contrast ratios, focus indicators, screen reader labels)
  - Dark Mode (if applicable: token overrides, opt-in or system-default)
  - Open Questions (unresolved design decisions)
</output_format>

<constraints>
- Be specific to THIS project, not generic. Design tokens must reflect the domain aesthetics.
- Design tokens must be specific values: hex colors (not just "use blue"), rem sizes, ms durations.
- Every screen in the Screen Inventory must map to a route from 03_frontend_lead.md.
- Every screen must reference which persona from 01_product_manager.md primarily uses it.
- Wireframes must be included — even rough ASCII art or a Mermaid diagram is required.
- Interaction patterns must include timing values (e.g., "200ms ease-in-out for hover transitions").
- Accessibility section must include actual contrast ratios for text-on-background combinations.
- Cross-reference 03_frontend_lead.md for component architecture alignment.
- Cross-reference 01_product_manager.md personas to ensure every persona has at least one primary screen.
- Color palette must pass WCAG 2.1 AA (4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text).
</constraints>

